# Example pre-snapshot hook for pre-snapshot.sh.
#
# Install at /etc/cockpit-nspawn/pull/<container-name>.hook on the SOURCE
# host, mode 600 if it contains anything sensitive, owned by root. A single
# shell command (or short script) run inside the container (via systemd-run,
# or nsenter when the container has no systemd of its own - see
# pre-snapshot.sh) right before the vault's pull. Optional - if this file
# doesn't exist, pre-snapshot.sh just skips it for that container - not
# every container needs one.
#
# The output file MUST be exactly /var/tmp/cockpit-nspawn-db.sql - that is
# the one path pull.sh's rsync explicitly includes (see pull-host.sh's/
# pull.sh's RSYNC_EXCLUDES, "--include=/var/tmp/cockpit-nspawn-db.sql"
# before the broader "--exclude=/var/tmp/*"); anything else written here
# never reaches the vault at all, no error, no warning. The dump is removed
# from the container again by restore-after-backup.sh after the pull.
#
# Examples:
#   ipa-backup
#   pg_dumpall -U postgres > /var/tmp/cockpit-nspawn-db.sql
#   # add --oids only if this specific database still has tables created
#   # with WITH OIDS (old PostgreSQL default, removed in PG 12+) - pg_dump/
#   # pg_dumpall otherwise silently drops those columns from the dump.
pg_dumpall -U postgres > /var/tmp/cockpit-nspawn-db.sql
